<title>JAPAN: Japan March vehicle exports up 9.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan March vehicle exports up 9.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle exports in March rose 9.3 percent from a year earlier to 356,137 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association said.</p>
<p>It was the 10th successive month in which exports rose on a year-on-year basis.</p>
<p>Exports in the year which ended on March 31 rose 6.2 percent the previous year to 3,847,865 units.</p>
<p>It was the first yearly export increase in five years.  </p>
<p>But in dollar terms, exports of assembled vehicles and vehicle components in 1996/97 fell 1.2 percent from a year earlier to $78.34 billion. They were down 1.7 percent in March from a year earlier at $6.95 billion.</p>
<p>Exports to the United States in 1996/97 marked their first gain in two years and those to the European Union their first in six years, the association said.</p>
<p>But exports in 1996/97 to Asia marked their first decline in two years, it said.  </p>
<p>Japan's 1996/97 exports were as follows with percentage</p>
<p>changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> Cars	 2,967,568  up     7.5 percent</p>
<p> Trucks	 835,330  up     1.9 percent</p>
<p> Buses	   44,967  up     3.0 percent</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of 1996/97 exports by major</p>
<p>destination, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> North America    1,244,837  up  5.9 percent</p>
<p> - U.S.	     1,169,520  up  5.3 percent</p>
<p> Europe total	 972,739  up  5.8 percent</p>
<p> - EU		   818,008  up  3.0 percent</p>
<p> Asia		   606,415  down 4.0 percent</p>
<p> Latin America	303,883  up   7.1 percent</p>
<p> Oceania		267,357  up   2.1 percent</p>
<p> Middle East	  301,289  up  41.6 percent</p>
<p> Africa		 140,922  up   6.6 percent</p>
<p>Exports by the five major Japanese manufacturers in 1996/97</p>
<p>with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> Toyota Motor	1,311,581  up   12.4 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	  598,244  up    0.8 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	   463,515  up    8.6 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors   462,077  down  5.0 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	   407,020  up    6.7 percent</p>
<p> Suzuki Motor	  201,112  up    7.2 percent</p>
<p> Isuzu Motors	  190,623  down  5.9 percent</p>
<p> Fuji Heavy	     83,352  up   34.1 percent</p>
<p> Daihatsu Motor	 75,061  up   16.2 percent</p>
<p> Hino Motors	    32,923  up    7.9 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Diesel	  22,357  up    4.1 percent</p>
<p>The breakdown of March exports is as follows with</p>
<p>percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> Cars	 267,069   up     9.8 percent</p>
<p> Trucks	84,096   up     8.2 percent</p>
<p> Buses	  4,972   up     2.1 percent</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of March exports by major</p>
<p>destination, with percentage changes from a year earlier:</p>
<p> North America    108,555   up     10.4 percent</p>
<p> - U.S.	     100,588   up	9.5 percent</p>
<p> Europe total	90,405   up	9.4 percent</p>
<p> - EU		  74,246   up	6.9 percent</p>
<p> Asia		  57,882   down    5.1 percent</p>
<p> Latin America     33,307   up     40.9 percent</p>
<p> Oceania	     21,060   down    6.2 percent</p>
<p> Africa		15,326   up     12.5 percent</p>
<p> Middle East	 28,669   up     21.8 percent</p>
